ng":0},"body":"<!-- Please search existing issues to avoid creating duplicates -->\n<!-- Please attach logs to help us diagnose your issue -->\n\n- Copilot Chat Extension Version: 0.27.2\n- VS Code Version: 1.100.2\n- OS Version: MacOS Sequoia 15.5\n- Feature (e.g. agent/edit/ask mode): ask mode\n- Selected model (e.g. GPT 4.1, Claude 3.7 Sonnet): Claude 3.7 Sonnet\n- Logs: ```The JS/TS language service crashed 5 times in the last 5 Minutes. This may be caused by a plugin contributed by one of these extensions: GitHub.copilot-chat Please try disabling these extensions before filing an issue against VS Code.```\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\n1. Open VS Code.\n2. Navigate to any TypeScript file (e.g., a React component).\n3. Attempt to trigger autocompletion:\n - Try to create an array variable.\n - Try accessing the properties of that array.\n - Try viewing available methods on an array (e.g., `.push()`, `.concat()`, `.map()`).\n4. Observe that the autocompletion list is missing standard JavaScript/TypeScript methods and properties.\n\n### Expected Behavior:\n\nAutocompletion should suggest all available methods, including standard JS/TS ones, such as `push()`, `map()`, and `concat()`.\n\n### Actual Behavior:\n\nThe language service fails to provide completions for standard methods. Only some contextual props appear (like component props), but core JS/TS completions are missing entirely.\n\n### Additional Notes:\n\nThe issue started occurring after updating VS Code to version 1.100.2. Disabling the GitHub Copilot Chat extension resolves the problem, which suggests a conflict between this extension and the JS/TS language service.\n\n### Evidence:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b4cf38cd-975b-4bb3-8ad2-ecbb0b5aaa41)\n","closed_by":{"login":"mjbvz","id":12821956,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIxOTU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12821956?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjbvz","html_url":"https://github.com/m